    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d784">

                <pb facs="0813" n="499" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg499"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.115 St 2/11</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Spring
                        Rice</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Memorandum</hi>
                </p>
                <p>His Majesty’s Ambassador presents his compliments to the Secretary of State of
                    the United States and has the honour to state that, according to information
                    which has reached His Majesty’s Government, two German oil steamships lying at
                    Baton Rouge, the <hi rendition="#italic">Chatham</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Standard</hi>, which belonged to the German-American
                    Company of Hamburg, have been sold to the Standard Oil Company of New Jersey and
                    their names changed to <hi rendition="#italic">Montano</hi> and <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caloria</hi> respectively.</p>
                <p>His Majesty’s Ambassador is instructed to say that His Majesty’s Government
                    consider themselves entitled to seize these ships on the ground that the sale
                    was effected only in order to escape risk of capture.</p>
                <closer>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">British Embassy</hi>,</closer>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                        calendar="gregorian" when="1914-10-17">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">October 17, 1914</hi>.</date>
                    <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received October 19</hi>.] </dateline>
            </div>
        </body>
